# AADAM pattern styles (owned references)

Jack owns the reference patterns in `assets/`. When creating or changing animal patterns in AADAM, **use these styles** — not generic standing-quadruped templates unless the animal clearly matches a different family already in the app (e.g. fox).

## Read first

Full construction notes: `assets/REFERENCE-STYLE.md`  
Extracted text: `assets/*.txt` next to each PDF

## Style families (current set)

| Family | Files | Pose / build |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Kitten | `KittenKaya.pdf` | Sitting; JAYG limbs; **3D cone ears** (Rule C; flat only if requested); sculpted head; thin tube tail |
| Teddy | `PatternTeddyBear.pdf` | Sitting; JAYG limbs; sew-on snout; folded dome ears; round MR feet; tiny ball tail |
| Unicorn | `PatternMollytheUnicorn.pdf` | Sitting; jointed/sewn hoof limbs; sculpted head; thin horn; spiral mane & tail |
| Hippo | `PatternHippoHarry.pdf` | Sitting; chain-oval muzzle→head one piece; legs continue into body; JAYG arms; chain tail |
| Chinchilla | `PatternChinchilla.pdf` | Sitting; head+body one piece; JAYG feet & fur tail; sew-on arms; fur-edged ears |
| Deer | `reference-deer.webp` | Dangling chibi; pear body; 2 arms + 2 legs; sew-on muzzle; antlers |
| Otter | (geometry template) | Floppy seated; sphere head + sew-on oval muzzle; paddle feet; thick tail backrest |

## Rules when Jack asks for a pattern

1. Pick the **closest family** above (or the exact animal if it already has a path).
2. Match that family’s piece list, join order, head/face method, and proportions.
3. Scale with the user’s SPI/RPI and total height.
4. **Detail bar:** every pattern must read like Kaya/Harry — exact rounds, placement cues, stuffing notes, precise joins, clean assembly. Not a vague template.
5. Prefer chenille/sitting-plush look: large head (~35–45% height), no long neck tube, no four stilts under a horizontal body — unless the animal is intentionally a standing quadruped (fox, horse, etc.).
6. When Jack adds a new owned PDF later: copy to `assets/`, extract `.txt`, update `REFERENCE-STYLE.md`, and wire that animal’s generator path.

## Do not

- Default every land mammal to standing deer/horse stilts.
- Invent a new construction style when an owned family already fits.
- Ignore `assets/REFERENCE-STYLE.md` when editing `js/animalGenerator.js` or `js/shapes.js`.
- Rely on animal **name alone** for new/ambiguous species — prefer an explicit **Style family** UI choice (Auto + the six families above) so “rabbit” does not silently become stilts or the wrong head method.
